# .ccls — ccls language-server configuration for RayguiObjC.
#
# Mirrors the macOS compile flags in Makefile: clang, Cocoa
# Foundation, no ARC, C11 for the wrapper sources.
#
# `-x objective-c` is global on purpose: without it clang parses this
# project's headers (RayguiObjC.h) as plain C and fails on `@interface`.
# Objective-C is a strict superset of C, so the vendored raylib .c files
# still index correctly under it.
#
# On Linux/GNUstep, Foundation flags from `gnustep-config --objc-flags`
# would need to be added here instead of relying on the system SDK.

clang
-x
objective-c
-Wall
-DPLATFORM_DESKTOP
-DGRAPHICS_API_OPENGL_33
-DGL_SILENCE_DEPRECATION
-Isrc
-Ivendor/raygui/src
-Ivendor/raylib/src
-Ivendor/raylib/src/external
-Ivendor/raylib/src/external/glfw/include

# Wrapper sources: manual retain/release, C11 — exactly what Makefile passes.
%objective-c%
-fno-objc-arc
-std=c11
